WEBVTT

00:00:06.124 --> 00:00:07.430
[man] This way.

00:00:29.408 --> 00:00:30.453
[growls]

00:00:33.281 --> 00:00:35.414
[Toothless growling]

00:00:45.642 --> 00:00:48.209
[roaring]

00:00:49.646 --> 00:00:51.517
Set sail!

00:00:51.691 --> 00:00:54.477
We head
for Helheim's Gate.

00:01:03.094 --> 00:01:05.313
Lead us home, devil.

00:01:26.204 --> 00:01:27.335
It's a mess.

00:01:28.989 --> 00:01:32.253
You must feel horrible.
You've lost everything:

00:01:32.427 --> 00:01:35.213
your father, your tribe,
your best friend.

00:01:35.387 --> 00:01:37.432
Thank you
for summing that up.

00:01:39.130 --> 00:01:41.088
Why couldn't I
have killed that dragon

00:01:41.262 --> 00:01:42.525
when I found him
in the woods?

00:01:42.699 --> 00:01:44.788
Would have been better
for everyone.

00:01:44.962 --> 00:01:47.442
Yep. The rest of us
would've done it.

00:01:48.226 --> 00:01:50.228
So why didn't you?

00:01:53.013 --> 00:01:53.884
Why didn't you?

00:01:54.058 --> 00:01:55.886
I don't know.

00:01:56.060 --> 00:01:58.149
- I couldn't.
- That's not an answer.

00:01:58.323 --> 00:02:00.847
Why is this
so important to you
all of a sudden?

00:02:01.021 --> 00:02:04.068
Because I want to remember
what you say right now.

00:02:04.242 --> 00:02:06.244
Oh, for the love of...
I was a coward.

00:02:06.418 --> 00:02:09.900
I was weak.
I wouldn't kill a dragon.

00:02:10.074 --> 00:02:13.294
- You said "wouldn't"
that time.
- Whatever! I wouldn't!

00:02:13.468 --> 00:02:17.385
Three hundred years,
and I'm the first Viking
who wouldn't kill a dragon.

00:02:21.955 --> 00:02:23.566
First to ride one, though.

00:02:26.090 --> 00:02:27.308
So...?

00:02:30.137 --> 00:02:33.488
I wouldn't kill him
because he looked
as frightened as I was.

00:02:34.577 --> 00:02:38.189
I looked at him
and I saw myself.

00:02:40.234 --> 00:02:42.454
I bet he's really
frightened now.

00:02:42.628 --> 00:02:44.369
What are you going
to do about it?

00:02:45.457 --> 00:02:48.503
Eh, probably
something stupid.

00:02:48.678 --> 00:02:50.505
Good, but you've
already done that.

00:02:52.246 --> 00:02:54.292
Then something crazy.

00:02:55.293 --> 00:02:57.425
That's more like it.

00:03:05.782 --> 00:03:08.959
[Stoick] Sound your positions.
Stay within earshot.

00:03:09.133 --> 00:03:12.092
- [man] Here!
- [man 2] One length
to your stern.

00:03:12.266 --> 00:03:17.010
Stoick, I was overhearing
some of the men just now,
and, well, some of them

00:03:17.184 --> 00:03:20.927
are wondering what it is
we're up to here.
Not me, of course.

00:03:21.101 --> 00:03:23.495
I know you're always the man
with the plan. But some,

00:03:23.669 --> 00:03:27.020
not me, are wondering
if there is, in fact,
a plan at all

00:03:27.194 --> 00:03:29.240
and what it might be.

00:03:29.414 --> 00:03:30.894
Find the nest and take it.

00:03:31.068 --> 00:03:33.113
Oh, of course.
Send them running.

00:03:33.287 --> 00:03:35.072
The old Viking fallback.
Nice and simple.

00:03:35.246 --> 00:03:36.639
- [gurgling]
- Shh, shh!

00:03:40.033 --> 00:03:41.644
[gurgling]

00:03:45.125 --> 00:03:46.649
Step aside.

